--TEST--
an attribute's name is placed by its prefix like any other name reference — `rule:programs/autoload` and `rule:programs/one-declaration-per-autoloaded-file`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `App\Audit` is written in exactly one place in this program: the `#[...]`
// group on `App\Handler`. It reaches no annotation, no `extends`, no
// `implements` and no expression, so the prefix lookup can only find
// `src/Audit.nvs` if the name harvest reads an attribute.
//
// That the file is *loaded* is what § 2's one-declaration rule then reports
// on: `src/Audit.nvs` carries a second top-level class, and the E0317 below
// can be reached from nowhere else. A class nothing loads is not checked.
require './src/Bootstrap.nvs';
echo App\Handler::run(), "\n";
--FILE src/Bootstrap.nvs--
<?nvs
autoload 'App' from './';
--FILE src/Handler.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App;

// Harvested from an autoloaded file, not the entry point, so this also pins
// that the map keeps being consulted as the worklist drains.
#[Audit]
class Handler
{
    public static function run(): string
    {
        return "handler";
    }
}
--FILE src/Audit.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App;

// A shape-typed `type` alias, which is what `rule:attributes/attach-sites-and-forms` makes an
// attribute's name: the harvest is the same prefix lookup either way, and
// what it looks a name up *for* is not `rule:programs/no-runtime-autoload`'s question.
type Audit = {};

class Smuggled
{
    public static function of(): string
    {
        return "smuggled";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0317]: an autoloaded file declares exactly one thing, named `App\Audit`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
